# 🪢 Rakhi for Anna ❤️

A cute and heartfelt Raksha Bandhan digital surprise created specially for my brother.

This isn't just a Raksha Bandhan greeting — it's a small interactive journey through our sibling bond, from childhood memories and silly fights to his caring heart, support, and everything I don't always say out loud. 🥹❤️

---

## 🌸 About the Project

**Rakhi for Anna** is a personal single-page interactive website created as a Raksha Bandhan gift for my brother.

The website combines:

- 🧸 Childhood memories
- 😂 Funny sibling fights
- 😤 Teasing and annoying each other
- 🛡️ His protective nature
- ❤️ His caring heart
- 🫶 His support and love
- 🌱 Growing up together
- 💌 A personal letter
- 🪢 Raksha Bandhan celebration
- 🤝 A promise from sister to brother
- 🏆 Fun "Brother Awards"
- ✨ Cute animations and illustrations

The goal is to make the experience feel like opening a small digital storybook made especially for him.

---

## ✨ Features

### 🌸 Interactive Opening

The website begins with:

> **Hey Anna... ❤️**

followed by a surprise button that starts the journey.

### 🧸 Childhood Story

A nostalgic section about growing up together and the memories created along the way.

### 😂 Sibling Fights

A playful section celebrating all the silly arguments, teasing, blaming and annoying moments that come with being siblings.

### 🛡️ Caring Heart

A heartfelt section highlighting the small ways a brother shows that he cares.

### ❤️ Little Things That Matter

The website talks about the little gestures that often mean more than words:

- Checking if I'm okay
- Giving advice
- Helping when needed
- Making me laugh
- Looking out for me
- Being there when it matters

### 🫶 Brother Cards

Interactive cards describe him as:

- My Protector
- My Professional Annoyer
- My Emergency Problem Solver
- My Personal Teaser
- My Support System
- My Brother
- My Forever Family

### 🌱 Growing Together

A section reflecting on watching each other grow from childhood to the present day.

### 💌 Personal Letter

The emotional centerpiece of the website is a handwritten-style letter dedicated to my brother.

### 🪢 Raksha Bandhan Moment

A special Rakhi section celebrates the meaning behind the festival and the bond between brother and sister.

### 🤝 Sister's Promise

A heartfelt promise about always being there for my brother regardless of how much life changes.

### 🏆 Official Brother Awards

A fun collection of brother awards such as:

- 🏆 Best Protector
- 😂 Best Annoyer
- 🛡️ Best Bodyguard
- 🫶 Best Support System
- 😤 Best Professional Teaser
- 🫡 Best Problem Solver
- ❤️ Biggest Softie
- ♾️ Best Brother — Forever

### ✨ Final Celebration

The website ends with:

> **Happy Raksha Bandhan, Anna! 🪢🌸**

and a final message from his little sister.

---

## 🎨 Design

The website uses a soft, warm and cute aesthetic inspired by a digital greeting card and illustrated storybook.

### Color Palette

- 🌸 Soft Pink
- 🤍 Cream
- 🍑 Peach
- ❤️ Warm Red
- 🍷 Burgundy
- ✨ Subtle Gold

The design focuses on:

- Rounded cards
- Soft shadows
- Handwritten-style typography
- Gentle animations
- Cute illustrations
- Warm and nostalgic visuals

---

## 💻 Technologies Used

- HTML5
- CSS3
- JavaScript
- SVG illustrations
- CSS animations
- Responsive Web Design
- Google Fonts

No backend or database is required.

---

## 📱 Responsive Design

The website is designed to work across:

- 📱 Mobile phones
- 💻 Laptops
- 🖥️ Desktop screens
- 📟 Tablets

Special attention is given to mobile viewing because the website is intended to be shared digitally.

---

## ♿ Accessibility

The website includes support for:

- Keyboard-friendly interactions
- Reduced motion preferences
- Responsive typography
- Readable color combinations
- Accessible interactive elements

Users who enable `prefers-reduced-motion` will receive a reduced-animation experience.

